[What will you be involved in?]
Participated in the development of next-generation 3D/4D Reconstruction Foundation Model and Gaussian Splatting, researching unified geometry, dynamic modeling, and high-fidelity renderable scene representations for real autonomous driving scenarios. 
The team possesses thousand-card-level GPU computing resources and large-scale real autonomous driving multi-camera and multi-timing data. Outstanding research achievements support further accumulation and submission to top conferences such as CVPR, ICCV, ECCV, NeurIPS, ICLR, and SIGGRAPH. 
[Core Directions]
Feed-Forward 3D/4D Reconstruction：D4RT、VGGT、PI3、DUSt3R / MASt3R； 
3D Gaussian Splatting / Neural Rendering: Feed-Forward Gaussian, Dynamic / 4D Gaussian, large-scale scene reconstruction; 
Unified 3D/4D representation and long temporal modeling: Depth, Point Map, Camera Pose, Tracking/Correspondence, Sparse Attention, Memory, Streaming Reconstruction; 
Explore the unified modeling and autonomous driving digital world building of the Reconstruction × Gaussian × Generative Model. 
[We look forward to you]
Master's/PhD students in computer vision, computer graphics, machine learning, robotics, or related fields; 
Familiar with PyTorch, Transformer, 3D Vision/Neural Rendering; 
Experience in 3D/4D Reconstruction, 3DGS, NeRF, Depth, Tracking, or Vision Foundation Model research is preferred.

[What will you be involved in?]
Participated in the development of the Generative World Model for autonomous driving, researching predictive and generative future world modeling capabilities, providing a generative world model foundation for autonomous driving training, simulation, and decision learning. 
The team possesses thousand-card-level GPU computing resources and massive amounts of real multi-camera autonomous driving video and timing data. Outstanding research achievements support further accumulation and submission to top conferences such as CVPR, ICCV, ECCV, NeurIPS, ICML, and ICR. 
[Core Directions]
Video Generation: Video Diffusion, DiT, Flow Matching, multi-camera video generation; 
Action-Conditioned World Model: Ego Action, scene state, and future world evolution modeling; 
Long-Horizon World Model: Causal / Streaming Generation, Memory, and the integration of World Model with VLA / Policy Learning. 
[We look forward to you]
Master's/PhD students in computer vision, machine learning, generative models, or related fields; 
Familiar with PyTorch, Transformer, Diffusion / DiT / Flow Matching; 
Experience in Video Generation, World Model, VLA, or Generative Modeling research is preferred.

