Responsibilities
1. Mission and Vision: 
We are building embodied systems for operational, mobile, and long-range tasks, with the World Model as the cognitive core, connecting the complete chain from multimodal perception, hidden space dynamics, planning and control to real-time execution, and constructing a unified world model: continuous observation, memory, prediction, reasoning, and action. You will stand on two fronts simultaneously: the model determines the upper limit of intelligence, while the AI Infra determines whether intelligence can be trained, deployed, and self-evolve through iteration. 
II. Job Responsibilities: 
1. World Model architecture design
Exploring the transfer and unification of video generation, hidden space dynamics, Flow Matching / Diffusion, VLA, and learnable memory in embodied scenarios. Breaking through the "open-loop imitation + post-fact" paradigm, models gain the ability to predict contact, occlusion, failure, and long-tail physics and reasoning counterfactually, evolving toward a unified world model. 
2. Closed loop between models and algorithms
Design a trainable, scalable world model and policy interface: representation learning, rolling prediction, planning (MPC / sampling / value guidance), and joint training with VLAs. Provide reproducible training schemes for long durations, sparse rewards, and multi-machine multi-task migration. 
3. AI infrastructure construction
Build embodied intelligent training and inference infrastructure from 0 to 1 or 1 to 100: multimodal data lakes, alignment and slicing of trajectories and videos, distributed training (multi-machine multi-card, mixed precision, fault tolerance and elasticity), simulation-real machine data return, evaluation and experiment management systems. Make every iteration reproducible, comparable, and rollable. 
4. Review and data flywheel
Deeply involved in simulation and real device evaluation systems: prediction errors, planning success rates, contact stability, and long-tail scenario coverage. Efficient feedback is established between simulation closed loops, remote operation data, and real machine failure cases, using data to drive the next priority of models and infrastructure. 
5. Software-hardware collaboration from training to deployment
Focusing on edge and station computing power, it completes the distillation, quantization, compilation, and scheduling of world models, collaborating with embedded and compiler teams. Under real latency, power consumption, and memory constraints, it balances predicted quality and control frequency, enabling laboratory capabilities to become mass-producible robotic products. 

