Job description
Taking on the responsibility of establishing, implementing, and executing a total quality assurance strategy for Onboard (Ubuntu/QNX) systems, application software, and embedded firmware products, you need to deeply understand product requirements and design, create and execute effective testing solutions (including manual and automated testing), identify, report, and track defects, with the ultimate goal of significantly reducing production environment bugs, eliminating unnecessary rollbacks, and improving software release quality and user satisfaction. You will work closely with the development team to promote the leftward shift in testing and advocate a quality-first culture. 
Key responsibilities
1. Execute the test content; 
2. Design high-quality, high-coverage test cases and test data, conduct in-depth analysis of product requirements and design documents, identify testing needs and risk points, and pay attention to program stability, resource usage, OTA scenarios, and other aspects; 
3. Plan and build automated testing capabilities, evaluate the satisfaction of open-source tools with current business needs, build automated toolchains (SIL/HIL/VIL) on demand, achieve automated high-frequency regression testing and report output, and improve the approval rate of all stages for issuance; 
4. Build and implement a quality system, clarify standard paths for requirements review→ test case design→ version testing → release, establish defect grading standards and release rules, and configure appropriate defect tracking and workflows; 
5. Promote the development team to develop a quality-first collaborative habit, establish a viable testing process within one quarter, and significantly reduce defect rates in production environments within six months. 
Job Requirements
1. 1-3 years of testing experience, independently responsible for embedded product or Linux system testing; 
2. Experience developing automated test scripts using Python or other scripting languages (such as Shell), not limited to C++/Python/Shell or API testing tools (Postman, RestAssured, pytest, etc.); 
3. Familiar with basic Linux/git commands, network protocols, multithreading/concurrency, basic database (SQL) testing, and understanding of basic performance and security testing concepts or tools; 
4. Familiar with CI/CD integration (Jenkins, GitLab CI, etc.), experience using version control tools (Git), and familiar with agile development processes (Scrum, Kanban); 
5. Familiar with common embedded development toolchains (such as GCC cross-compilation toolchain, OpenOCD, JTAG debugger); experience in full-vehicle OTA upgrade testing is preferred.

