Company Introduction: 
WeRide was founded in 2017 and is a global leader in L4-level autonomous driving technology. It is dedicated to "transforming human travel through driverless driving." It has conducted autonomous driving R&D, testing, and operations in more than 25 cities worldwide, accumulating over 16 million kilometers of autonomous driving mileage. Its application scenarios cover smart mobility, smart freight, and smart sanitation, forming five major product portfolios: autonomous taxis, autonomous minibuses, autonomous freight vehicles, autonomous sanitation vehicles, and advanced intelligent driving. It offers a variety of services including ride-hailing, on-demand buses, intra-city freight, intelligent sanitation, and advanced intelligent driving solutions. 
With a diversified commercialization strategy of "1 platform + 3 major scenarios + 5 major products," WeRide leads in commercial revenue among similar autonomous driving companies and has established strategic partnerships with many top global OEMs and tier-one suppliers, including Renault-Nissan-Mitsubishi Alliance, Yutong Group, Bosch, and GAC Group, continuously providing more new options for human mobility. 
Introduction to the Data team: 
In industries like autonomous vehicles, the importance of data is self-evident, especially as models grow larger and algorithm modeling processes gradually shift from data-driven to data-centric, data processing is receiving increasing attention. 
The main responsibility of the Data Group is to connect the closed-loop data chain for autonomous driving, including data collection, data indexing, data mining, data annotation, model training, and more, creating a complete closed loop and accelerating the iteration of autonomous driving algorithms. At the same time, the Data Group has also developed multiple data analysis and processing toolchains, comprehensively building an enterprise-level big data platform. 
Introduction to the Automated Annotation Group: 
In data processing, data annotation is a crucial part. We hope to add more intelligence to traditional manual annotation, allowing models to automatically and semi-automatically complete data annotation, solving issues such as cost, efficiency, and data quality in manual annotation, and powerfully "empowering" the business. 
Unlike model development in specific business scenarios, the annotation stage has more abundant computing resources and richer data, allowing for the selection of larger and newer models (including large models), and also human-in-the-loop — these unique features are very interesting and, more importantly, key reasons why automated annotation can be realized. 
Job Responsibilities: 
We are seeking an automated annotation engineer responsible for designing and developing automated and semi-automated annotation algorithms for autonomous driving, collaborating with the annotation tool development team to develop optimization solutions. Core responsibilities include: 
Design and develop automated and semi-automated annotation algorithms for autonomous driving data to improve annotation efficiency and accuracy, including but not limited to: point cloud detection/recognition/segmentation, image detection/recognition/segmentation, etc.; 
Collaborate with the annotation tool development team to develop optimization solutions for annotation tools to improve their usability and functionality; 
Research and explore new automated annotation technologies and algorithms to continuously improve the efficiency and accuracy of data annotation. 
Job Requirements: 
Master's degree or above in computer science, electronics, automation, applied mathematics, or related fields; 
Solid theoretical foundation in machine learning and deep learning, solid mathematical foundation, and problem-solving skills; 
Solid Python/C++ development skills and good programming habits; 
In-depth research and development experience in at least one of LiDAR/image/fusion target detection, target tracking, 3D reconstruction, video analysis, NLP, and other technologies; 
Good communication skills, strong team spirit, and strong research spirit; 
Bonus Points: Experience in developing autonomous driving perception algorithms is preferred; 
Bonus items: Priority given to model fine-tuning, active learning, and reinforcement learning R&D experience.

