Job Positioning: 
As the head of HMI in the intelligent driving product team, you will lead the design and implementation of interaction logic, information transmission, state awareness, and takeover experience between autonomous driving systems and drivers. Your work directly affects users' trust, sense of security, and willingness to use intelligent driving systems, serving as a key bridge connecting technical capabilities and user experience. 
Core Responsibilities: 
1. Conduct in-depth research on intelligent driving HMI requirements in truck/logistics scenarios, analyze driver cognitive load, attention allocation, takeover responses under different automation levels (L2–L4), and identify HMI design pain points; 
2. Define the overall strategy and interaction framework for intelligent driving HMI, including but not limited to: 
System status visualization (such as ACC/LKA/NOA status, ODD boundaries, functional availability)
Risk Early Warning and Tiered Prompt Mechanism (Visual, Auditory, and Tactile Multimodal Feedback)
Design and timeliness verification of takeover request processes
3. Output HMI product requirements documents (PRD), interactive prototypes, state machine logic diagrams, and acceptance criteria, and work closely with the UX/UI team to ensure the design solution is feasible, testable, and compliant with ergonomic principles; 
4. Participate in formulating human-machine collaboration strategies for intelligent driving functions, promote deep coupling between HMI and perception, planning, control, and other modules to ensure interaction logic aligns with system capabilities; 
5. Lead real-vehicle/simulation testing and user evaluation of HMI functions, quantifying interaction effects through eye tracking, handover time, subjective surveys, and other methods, continuously iterating and optimizing; 
6. Cross-departmental collaboration: Collaborate with algorithm, software, testing, cockpit electronics, and functional safety teams to ensure HMI design meets safety, compliance, and engineering constraints; 
7. Establish an HMI data indicator system (such as prompt efficiency, misoperation rate, takeover response time), and optimize interaction strategies through actual vehicle operation data; 
8. Support customer demonstrations, regulatory certification, and marketing, write HMI function description materials, and clearly communicate interaction concepts and value to customers and partners. 
Job Requirements: 
1. Bachelor's degree or above in automotive engineering, human factors engineering, industrial design, computer science, psychology, or a related field; 
2. Over 3 years of experience in intelligent cockpit or intelligent driving HMI products; experience in designing HMIs for commercial vehicles (heavy/light trucks) or logistics scenarios is preferred; 
3. Deep understanding of the HMI challenges of L2–L3 level autonomous driving, familiar with mainstream HMI architectures (dashboard/HUD/central control/voice/steering wheel light strips, etc.) and interaction paradigms; 
4. Possess solid user research and scenario analysis capabilities, able to transform complex technical logic into intuitive, secure, and low-interference interactive solutions; 
